<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Associated Domains, which is the iOS half of the deep link contract.

	STATUS, re-verified 6 October 2026 against the repository (directive D41,
	measure and never quote). An earlier version of this comment said the file
	was inert, that nothing in the project pointed at it, and that the
	association file carried a Team ID placeholder. All three were true on
	28 September and none is true now.

	1. THE PROJECT ADOPTS THIS FILE. `App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` sets
	   `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = App/App.entitlements` in both build
	   configurations (Debug and Release). It is no longer inert: every build
	   signs with these entitlements, so the capabilities must exist on the
	   App ID `com.vallospaces.app` or signing refuses.
	2. THE TEAM ID IS REAL. `apps/web/public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association`
	   carries `X74KD52994.com.vallospaces.app`, and `project.pbxproj` carries
	   `DevelopmentTeam = X74KD52994`. The file passes its own checker:
	   `node scripts/check-deep-links.mjs` run with the ios platform flag exits 0. Do not
	   enrol again and do not go looking for a placeholder to replace.
	3. A SIGNED APP STORE BUILD HAS ALREADY BEEN MADE. GitHub Actions run
	   37103086939 on 3 October 2026 ran `iOS signed archive (App Store)` to
	   success with this entitlements file in the project, and its export step
	   ran with destination upload, so the IPA went to App Store Connect.

	WHAT IS STILL OPEN, honestly. Whether Apple has verified the domain is
	UNKNOWN from the repository: check what Apple's CDN actually serves at
	https://app-site-association.cdn-apple.com/a/v1/www.vallospaces.com and
	expect a device to take up to a day to pick up a change. Whether the
	build has reached TestFlight testers is UNKNOWN from the repository. No
	device has ever run the build, so universal links are untested on
	hardware. The Android half is genuinely blocked: the two fingerprints in
	`assetlinks.json` are still placeholders.

	The Team ID is ten alphanumeric characters (Apple Developer, Membership
	details). It is NOT the Apple ID email and it is NOT the bundle
	identifier. During development, the `applinks:` entries can be suffixed
	with `?mode=developer` to bypass Apple's CDN, which is the only sane way
	to test a change to the association file.

	The one domain is `www.vallospaces.com`, the canonical host, matching the
	Android manifest. The apex is NOT claimed: `vallospaces.com` answers every
	path, `/.well-known/apple-app-site-association` included, with a 308 to www
	(Vercel's domain setting), and Apple's CDN does not follow redirects, so an
	apex entry could never verify. The reasoning and the way back are in the
	App Links note in `AndroidManifest.xml` ("THE APEX").
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:www.vallospaces.com</string>
		<!--
			FACE ID ON THE PASSCODE AND THE MONEY LOCK (7 October 2026, the
			founder: "set and build Face ID to work"). Vallo's biometric is a
			WebAuthn platform key verified on the server
			(`src/lib/passcode/passkey-unlock.ts`). WKWebView runs WebAuthn
			for a site only when the app is associated with it as a web
			credential, which is this entry plus the `webcredentials` block in
			`public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association`. The Associated
			Domains capability is already on the App ID (applinks above), so
			this needs no portal change; it needs a NATIVE REBUILD.
		-->
		<string>webcredentials:www.vallospaces.com</string>
	</array>

	<!--
		PUSH NOTIFICATIONS. The Apple account exists (see the note at the top
		of this file); what remains is the APNs key and the server variables.

		`aps-environment` is the entitlement that lets a build register with
		APNs at all. The project adopts this file, so a build fails outright
		with "provisioning profile does not include the aps-environment
		entitlement" unless the Push Notifications capability exists on the
		App ID `com.vallospaces.app`. Whether the APNs key and the APNS_*
		server variables are set is UNKNOWN from the repository (none were
		set on 28 September 2026).

		THE OWNER'S STEPS FOR PUSH, in order, none doable from this repository.

		1. Apple Developer Program membership, 99 USD a year. Already held:
		   the team is X74KD52994 (see the note at the top of this file).
		2. Certificates Identifiers and Profiles, the App ID
		   `com.vallospaces.app`, tick Push Notifications, save, let the
		   profiles regenerate.
		3. Keys, plus, a new key with Apple Push Notifications service (APNs)
		   ticked. Download the `.p8`. IT DOWNLOADS EXACTLY ONCE and cannot be
		   retrieved again; a lost one has to be revoked and replaced. Then
		   set APNS_KEY_ID (the key's 10 character id), APNS_TEAM_ID (the same
		   Team ID the note above describes finding) and APNS_PRIVATE_KEY (the
		   whole .p8 contents) in the server environment. NOT in this
		   repository: see `src/lib/push/credentials.ts`.
		4. Xcode, the App target, Signing and Capabilities, plus, Push
		   Notifications. Xcode adopts this file rather than creating a second
		   one and sets `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS` itself.

		THE VALUE BELOW IS `development` AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
		A build signed with a development profile receives a SANDBOX device
		token, and a sandbox token sent to the production gateway is refused
		400 BadDeviceToken, which reads exactly like a dead device and will
		have somebody retiring perfectly good tokens. `development` is what a
		local or TestFlight-from-Xcode build wants. AN APP STORE BUILD NEEDS
		THIS CHANGED TO `production`, and the server side switched with it by
		setting APNS_PRODUCTION=true. Xcode's automatic signing rewrites this
		for a Release archive, but the SERVER half does not change itself and
		is the half people forget.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>

	<!--
		SIGN IN WITH APPLE (STORE-02). Signing needs the App ID
		`com.vallospaces.app` to have the Sign In with Apple capability
		ticked in the Apple Developer portal (the 3 October 2026 signed
		archive succeeded, so it evidently does, or automatic signing added it). The app only draws the button
		when Supabase reports the Apple provider enabled AND the running
		binary carries the `SignInWithApple` plugin, so this entitlement being
		present early changes nothing a person can see.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
